# Settings for the github-app add-on: GitHub access as a GitHub App. Only the gateway
# reads this file; it holds no secret. The App's private key goes into github-app.pem
# next to it (mode 600) and is mounted only into the gateway, which mints installation
# tokens (valid 1 hour) for the agent. See addons/github-app/README.md.

# App ID (a number, on the App's settings page) or its Client ID (Iv23...)
GITHUB_APP_ID=
# The organization (or user) the App is installed on; its installation is looked up
# at the first request. Or give the installation ID directly (the number at the end of
# https://github.com/organizations/ORG/settings/installations/NUMBER).
GITHUB_APP_OWNER=
#GITHUB_APP_INSTALLATION_ID=
# Narrow each token below what the installation grants (optional, recommended when
# the App is installed on more repositories than this sandbox should touch).
# Repository names, space or comma separated ("owner/" is ignored):
GITHUB_APP_REPOSITORIES=
# Permissions as name:read|write, e.g. contents:write,pull_requests:write,issues:write
GITHUB_APP_PERMISSIONS=
# Commit identity inside the sandbox. Empty: the App's bot user
# ("my-app[bot]" <ID+my-app[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>), so commits link to it.
GITHUB_APP_AUTHOR_NAME=
GITHUB_APP_AUTHOR_EMAIL=
# GitHub Enterprise Server only: its host name (default github.com). Allowlisted by the
# gateway. The API is https://HOST/api/v3 unless GITHUB_APP_API_URL says otherwise.
#GITHUB_APP_HOST=
#GITHUB_APP_API_URL=
